  "id": "koza_rock",
  "name": "Koza rock (Okinawan base-town hard rock)",
  "family": "rock",
  "lineage": "Koza rock is the hard rock scene of Koza, now Okinawa City, beside Kadena Air Base, where bands played long sets of British and American hard rock in English for US servicemen in the bars of the Vietnam War years. Groups such as Condition Green and the organ-led Murasaki grew out of this circuit and recorded LPs in the 1970s.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1970s koza rock, distorted Rock, regional branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. humbucker electric guitar, electric bass, machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows full lathed both sides lathed drum kit, fast tremolo tonewheel organ. live tracking. shure SM57, console-strip pre, marshall super lead 1959, colored vintage console, parametric EQ. tape 15ips.",
